{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And how shall I do this great evil and sin against Elohim.</b> He indicated that he would commit two evils: the first, that he would be betraying his master who trusts in him — this is 'this great evil,' namely the betrayal he would commit against his master. The second, that he would be sinning against Elohim — and this is in the language of Scripture, which says concerning the sons of Eli (I Samuel 2:25): ״אם יחטא איש לאיש ופללו אלהים ואם לה' יחטא איש מי יתפלל לו״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:49.594056034Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}